IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026): part sga1, module 6.
-- Part 4, Division 3 (shares): ss 71 to 73B: alteration of share capital, validation of shares improperly issued, redenomination.
--
-- Every function answers MAYBE (BOOLEAN, NUMBER ...): JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sga1)") has the rule of 2026-10-29 and the two readings "for a lawyer".
-- A duty with a time limit is asked as "late" or "in default": JUST TRUE means the duty was not done in time.

§ `Section 71: power of company to alter its share capital`

-- (1) the five ways. Paragraph (a) is deleted. "Subject to subsections (1B) and (1C)": a private company alters by notice under (1B), taking effect as (1C) says; this function is the general-meeting route.
-- src:6904 | 71.—(1) Subject to subsections (1B) and (1C), a company, if so
-- src:6905 | authorised by its constitution, may in general meeting alter its share
-- src:6906 | capital in any one or more of the following ways:
-- src:6908 | (a) [Deleted by Act 21 of 2005]
-- src:6910 | (b) consolidate and divide all or any of its share capital;
-- src:6912 | (c) convert all or any of its paid‑up shares into stock and
-- src:6913 | reconvert that stock into paid‑up shares;
-- src:6915 | (d) subdivide its shares or any of them, so however that in the
-- src:6916 | subdivision the proportion between the amount paid and
-- src:6917 | the amount, if any, unpaid on each reduced share is the
-- src:6918 | same as it was in the case of the share from which the
-- src:6919 | reduced share is derived;
-- src:6924 | (e) cancel the number of shares which at the date of the
-- src:6925 | passing of the resolution in that behalf have not been taken
-- src:6926 | or agreed to be taken by any person or which have been
-- src:6927 | forfeited and diminish the amount of its share capital by the
-- src:6928 | number of the shares so cancelled.
@ref s 71(1) (src:6904-6928)
DECLARE `s 71(1) alteration` IS ONE OF
    `s 71(1)(b) consolidate and divide all or any of its share capital`
    `s 71(1)(c) convert all or any of its paid-up shares into stock and reconvert that stock into paid-up shares`
    `s 71(1)(d) subdivide its shares or any of them`
        HAS `s 71(1)(d) the proportion between the amount paid and the amount, if any, unpaid on each reduced share is the same as it was in the case of the share from which the reduced share is derived` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 71(1)(e) cancel the number of shares which have not been taken or agreed to be taken, or which have been forfeited, and diminish the share capital`
        HAS `s 71(1)(e) at the date of the passing of the resolution the shares have not been taken or agreed to be taken by any person, or have been forfeited` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 71(1) some other alteration`

@ref s 71(1) (src:6904-6928)
GIVEN `the constitution of the company authorises the company to alter its share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alteration is made in general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      alteration IS A `s 71(1) alteration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(1) the company may alter its share capital in the way` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the constitution of the company authorises the company to alter its share capital` AND `the alteration is made in general meeting`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a company, if so authorised by its constitution, may in general meeting alter its share capital" -- a grant whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1); the subsection does not say the company may not
    ELSE CONSIDER alteration
         WHEN `s 71(1)(b) consolidate and divide all or any of its share capital` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 71(1)(c) convert all or any of its paid-up shares into stock and reconvert that stock into paid-up shares` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 71(1)(d) subdivide its shares or any of them` proportion THEN (IF proportion THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "so however that in the subdivision the proportion between the amount paid and the amount, if any, unpaid on each reduced share is the same as it was in the case of the share from which the reduced share is derived" -- the power is given on that condition (grant ruling, limit 1)
         WHEN `s 71(1)(e) cancel the number of shares which have not been taken or agreed to be taken, or which have been forfeited, and diminish the share capital` untaken THEN (IF untaken THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "cancel the number of shares which at the date of the passing of the resolution in that behalf have not been taken or agreed to be taken by any person or which have been forfeited" -- other shares are not covered
         WHEN `s 71(1) some other alteration` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraphs (b) to (e) are listed without "only"

-- (1A) a public company's notice.
-- src:6932 | (1A) A public company which alters its share capital may lodge
-- src:6933 | with the Registrar a notice of the alteration in the prescribed form.
@ref s 71(1A) (src:6932-6933)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has altered its share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(1A) the public company may lodge with the Registrar a notice of the alteration` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` AND `the company has altered its share capital`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company which alters its share capital may lodge" -- a grant whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1); the subsection does not require the notice

-- (1B) a private company's alteration by notice.
-- src:6937 | (1B) A private company may alter its share capital by lodging a
-- src:6938 | notice of alteration in the prescribed form with the Registrar.
@ref s 71(1B) (src:6937-6938)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notice of alteration in the prescribed form has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(1B) the private company may alter its share capital by lodging the notice` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private company` AND `a notice of alteration in the prescribed form has been lodged with the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company may alter its share capital by lodging a notice of alteration in the prescribed form with the Registrar" -- a grant whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- (1C) the alteration by a private company does not take effect until the register is updated.
-- src:6942 | (1C) An alteration of share capital of a private company on or after
-- src:6943 | 3 January 2016 does not take effect until the electronic register of
-- src:6944 | members of the company is updated by the Registrar under
-- src:6945 | section 196A(5).
@ref s 71(1C) (src:6942-6945)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the alteration` IS A DATE
      `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(1C) the alteration has not yet taken effect` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company`) OR `the day of the alteration` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An alteration of share capital of a private company on or after 3 January 2016" -- a public company or an alteration before 3 January 2016 is not covered (periods ruling (c); fork F-X1)
    ELSE (IF `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not take effect until the electronic register of members of the company is updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)" -- the register has been updated, so the bar is over
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (2) a cancellation is not a reduction.
-- src:6951 | (2) A cancellation of shares under this section is not deemed to be a
-- src:6952 | reduction of share capital within the meaning of this Act.
@ref s 71(2) (src:6951-6952)
GIVEN `the cancellation of shares is made under section 71` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(2) the cancellation is deemed to be a reduction of share capital within the meaning of this Act` MEANS
    IF `the cancellation of shares is made under section 71`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A cancellation of shares under this section is not deemed to be a reduction of share capital within the meaning of this Act"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A cancellation of shares under this section" -- another cancellation is not covered

-- (3)(a) an unlimited company's increase of the issue price.
-- src:6956 | (3) An unlimited company having a share capital may by any
-- src:6957 | resolution passed for the purposes of section 30(1) —
-- src:6959 | (a) increase the amount of its share capital by increasing the
-- src:6960 | issue price of each of its shares, but subject to the condition
-- src:6961 | that no part of the increased capital is capable of being
-- src:6962 | called up except in the event and for the purposes of the
-- src:6963 | company being wound up; and
@ref s 71(3)(a) (src:6956-6963)
GIVEN `the company is an unlimited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has passed a resolution for the purposes of section 30(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no part of the increased capital is capable of being called up except in the event and for the purposes of the company being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(3)(a) the unlimited company may increase the amount of its share capital by increasing the issue price of each of its shares` MEANS
    IF    `the company is an unlimited company having a share capital`
      AND `the company has passed a resolution for the purposes of section 30(1)`
      AND `no part of the increased capital is capable of being called up except in the event and for the purposes of the company being wound up`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An unlimited company having a share capital may by any resolution passed for the purposes of section 30(1) -- (a) increase the amount of its share capital by increasing the issue price of each of its shares, but subject to the condition that no part of the increased capital is capable of being called up except in the event and for the purposes of the company being wound up" -- a grant whose gate or condition is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- (3)(b) the uncalled portion.
-- src:6956 | (3) An unlimited company having a share capital may by any
-- src:6957 | resolution passed for the purposes of section 30(1) —
-- src:6965 | (b) in addition or alternatively, provide that a specified portion
-- src:6966 | of its uncalled share capital is not capable of being called
-- src:6967 | up except in the event and for the purposes of the company
-- src:6968 | being wound up.
@ref s 71(3)(b) (src:6956-6968)
GIVEN `the company is an unlimited company having a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has passed a resolution for the purposes of section 30(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71(3)(b) the unlimited company may provide that a specified portion of its uncalled share capital is not capable of being called up except in a winding up` MEANS
    IF `the company is an unlimited company having a share capital` AND `the company has passed a resolution for the purposes of section 30(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An unlimited company having a share capital may by any resolution passed for the purposes of section 30(1) ... provide that a specified portion of its uncalled share capital is not capable of being called up" -- a grant whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1)

§ `Section 72: validation of shares improperly issued`

-- The Court's power.
-- src:6975 | 72. Where a company has purported to issue or allot shares and the
-- src:6976 | creation, issue or allotment of those shares was invalid by reason of
-- src:6977 | any provision of this or any other written law or of the constitution of
-- src:6978 | the company or otherwise or the terms of issue or allotment were
-- src:6979 | inconsistent with or unauthorised by any such provision the Court
-- src:6980 | may, upon application made by the company or by a holder or
-- src:6981 | mortgagee of any of those shares or by a creditor of the company and
-- src:6982 | upon being satisfied that in all the circumstances it is just and
-- src:6983 | equitable to do so, make an order validating the issue or allotment of
-- src:6984 | those shares or confirming the terms of issue or allotment thereof or
-- src:6985 | both and upon a copy of the order being lodged with the Registrar
-- src:6986 | those shares are deemed to have been validly issued or allotted upon
-- src:6987 | the terms of the issue or allotment thereof.
@ref s 72 (src:6975-6987)
GIVEN `the company has purported to issue or allot shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the creation, issue or allotment of the shares was invalid, or the terms of issue or allotment were inconsistent with or unauthorised by a provision of a written law or of the constitution of the company or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the company, by a holder or mortgagee of any of those shares or by a creditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that in all the circumstances it is just and equitable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72 the Court may make an order validating the issue or allotment of the shares or confirming the terms of issue or allotment` MEANS
    IF    `the company has purported to issue or allot shares`
      AND `the creation, issue or allotment of the shares was invalid, or the terms of issue or allotment were inconsistent with or unauthorised by a provision of a written law or of the constitution of the company or otherwise`
      AND `the application is made by the company, by a holder or mortgagee of any of those shares or by a creditor of the company`
      AND `the Court is satisfied that in all the circumstances it is just and equitable to do so`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a company has purported to issue or allot shares ... the Court may, upon application made by the company or by a holder or mortgagee of any of those shares or by a creditor of the company and upon being satisfied that in all the circumstances it is just and equitable to do so, make an order" -- a power whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- The deeming on lodgment of the order. Until the copy is lodged the text does not deem the shares validly issued.
@ref s 72 (src:6975-6987)
GIVEN `the Court has made an order validating the issue or allotment or confirming the terms of issue or allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 72 the shares are deemed to have been validly issued or allotted upon the terms of the issue or allotment` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Court has made an order validating the issue or allotment or confirming the terms of issue or allotment`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "upon a copy of the order being lodged with the Registrar those shares are deemed to have been validly issued" -- the deeming follows an order of the Court
    ELSE (IF `a copy of the order has been lodged with the Registrar`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon a copy of the order being lodged with the Registrar those shares are deemed to have been validly issued" -- an order made but its copy not yet lodged: the text makes lodgment the trigger (fork F-AL1)

§ `Section 73: redenomination of shares`

-- (1) the power, by ordinary resolution; subsection (9) lets the constitution exclude it.
-- src:6993 | 73.—(1) A company having a share capital may by ordinary
-- src:6994 | resolution convert its share capital or any class of shares from
-- src:6995 | one currency to another currency.
-- src:7053 | (9) A company’s constitution may exclude or restrict the exercise of
-- src:7054 | a power conferred by this section.
@ref s 73(1) (src:6993-7054)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has passed an ordinary resolution converting its share capital or a class of shares from one currency to another currency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the company excludes the exercise of the power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(1) the company may convert its share capital or a class of shares from one currency to another currency` MEANS
    IF `the constitution of the company excludes the exercise of the power`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company's constitution may exclude or restrict the exercise of a power conferred by this section" -- the constitution has excluded it (subsection (9); a restriction short of exclusion is for the caller to read)
    ELSE (IF `the company has a share capital` AND `the company has passed an ordinary resolution converting its share capital or a class of shares from one currency to another currency`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company having a share capital may by ordinary resolution convert" -- a grant whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- (2) what the resolution may authorise.
-- src:6999 | (2) A resolution under this section may authorise a company having
-- src:7000 | a share capital to redenominate its share capital —
-- src:7002 | (a) on more than one occasion; and
-- src:7004 | (b) at a specified time or under specified circumstances.
@ref s 73(2) (src:6999-7004)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is a resolution under section 73` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution authorises redenomination on more than one occasion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution authorises redenomination at a specified time or under specified circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(2) the resolution may authorise the company to redenominate its share capital as it does` MEANS
    IF    `the company has a share capital`
      AND `the resolution is a resolution under section 73`
      AND (`the resolution authorises redenomination on more than one occasion` OR `the resolution authorises redenomination at a specified time or under specified circumstances`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A resolution under this section may authorise a company having a share capital to redenominate its share capital -- (a) on more than one occasion; and (b) at a specified time or under specified circumstances" -- a grant whose gate is unmet (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- (3) the spot rate.
-- src:7008 | (3) The redenomination must be made at a spot rate of exchange
-- src:7009 | specified in the resolution.
@ref s 73(3) (src:7008-7009)
GIVEN `the redenomination is made at a spot rate of exchange specified in the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(3) the redenomination is made as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the redenomination is made at a spot rate of exchange specified in the resolution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The redenomination must be made at a spot rate of exchange specified in the resolution" (a duty not met, the subsection's own question)

-- (4) the two ways of fixing the rate.
-- src:7013 | (4) The rate mentioned in subsection (3) must be either —
-- src:7015 | (a) a rate prevailing on a day specified in the resolution; or
-- src:7017 | (b) a rate determined by taking the average of rates prevailing
-- src:7018 | on each consecutive day of a period specified in the
-- src:7019 | resolution.
@ref s 73(4) (src:7013-7019)
GIVEN `the rate is a rate prevailing on a day specified in the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rate is a rate determined by taking the average of rates prevailing on each consecutive day of a period specified in the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(4) the rate is one the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF `the rate is a rate prevailing on a day specified in the resolution` OR `the rate is a rate determined by taking the average of rates prevailing on each consecutive day of a period specified in the resolution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The rate mentioned in subsection (3) must be either -- (a) a rate prevailing on a day specified in the resolution; or (b) a rate determined by taking the average of rates prevailing on each consecutive day of a period specified in the resolution" (a duty not met, the subsection's own question)

-- (5) the day or period must fall in the 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed.
-- src:7026 | (5) The day or period specified for the purposes of subsection (4)
-- src:7027 | must be within the period of 28 days ending on the day before the
-- src:7028 | resolution is passed.
@ref s 73(5) (src:7026-7028)
GIVEN `the day specified for the purposes of subsection (4)` IS A DATE
      `the day the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(5) the day specified is within the period of 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is within a period before` `the day specified for the purposes of subsection (4)` `the day the resolution is passed` 28 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The day or period specified for the purposes of subsection (4) must be within the period of 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed" (a duty not met, the subsection's own question; keel convention P6)

@ref s 73(5) (src:7026-7028)
GIVEN `the first day of the period specified for the purposes of subsection (4)` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period specified for the purposes of subsection (4)` IS A DATE
      `the day the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(5) the period specified is within the period of 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed` MEANS
    IF    `period: the date is within a period before` `the first day of the period specified for the purposes of subsection (4)` `the day the resolution is passed` 28 Days
      AND `period: the date is within a period before` `the last day of the period specified for the purposes of subsection (4)` `the day the resolution is passed` 28 Days
      AND `the first day of the period specified for the purposes of subsection (4)` AT MOST `the last day of the period specified for the purposes of subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The day or period specified for the purposes of subsection (4) must be within the period of 28 days ending on the day before the resolution is passed" (a duty not met, the subsection's own question; keel convention P6)

-- (6) conditions in the resolution.
-- src:7032 | (6) A resolution under this section may specify conditions which
-- src:7033 | must be met before the redenomination takes effect.
@ref s 73(6) (src:7032-7033)
GIVEN `the resolution is a resolution under section 73` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution specifies conditions which must be met before the redenomination takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(6) the resolution may specify conditions which must be met before the redenomination takes effect` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is a resolution under section 73` AND `the resolution specifies conditions which must be met before the redenomination takes effect`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A resolution under this section may specify conditions" -- a power the resolution has not used, or a resolution not under section 73 (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- (7) when the redenomination takes effect: on the day the resolution is passed, or on a later day it determines, and only once the conditions of (6) are met.
-- src:7032 | (6) A resolution under this section may specify conditions which
-- src:7033 | must be met before the redenomination takes effect.
-- src:7037 | (7) Redenomination in accordance with a resolution under this
-- src:7038 | section takes effect —
-- src:7040 | (a) on the day on which the resolution is passed; or
-- src:7042 | (b) on such later day as may be determined in accordance with
-- src:7043 | the resolution.
@ref s 73(7) (src:7032-7043)
GIVEN `the day the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      `the resolution determines a later day on which the redenomination takes effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the later day determined in accordance with the resolution` IS A DATE
      `the conditions the resolution specifies under subsection (6) have been met, or it specifies none` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(7) the redenomination has taken effect` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the conditions the resolution specifies under subsection (6) have been met, or it specifies none`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "conditions which must be met before the redenomination takes effect" -- a condition of the resolution is unmet
    ELSE (IF `the day on which the question is asked` AT LEAST (IF `the resolution determines a later day on which the redenomination takes effect` THEN `the later day determined in accordance with the resolution` ELSE `the day the resolution is passed`)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "takes effect -- (a) on the day on which the resolution is passed; or (b) on such later day as may be determined in accordance with the resolution" -- that day has not come (a day fixed in the text's own words: periods ruling (a))

-- (8) lapse after 28 days beginning on the date the resolution is passed: the period ends 27 days after that date (the date itself is day 1).
-- src:7047 | (8) A resolution under this section lapses if the redenomination for
-- src:7048 | which it provides has not taken effect at the end of the period of
-- src:7049 | 28 days beginning on the date on which it is passed.
@ref s 73(8) (src:7047-7049)
GIVEN `the day the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      `the redenomination has taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the redenomination took effect` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(8) the resolution has lapsed` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN (`the day the resolution is passed` PLUS 27)
    THEN (IF `the redenomination has taken effect` AND `the day the redenomination took effect` AT MOST (`the day the resolution is passed` PLUS 27)
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "lapses if the redenomination for which it provides has not taken effect at the end of the period of 28 days" -- it took effect within the period
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the end of the period of 28 days beginning on the date on which it is passed" -- the period has not yet ended (a period the text fixes: periods ruling (a); fork F-AL2)

-- (9) the constitution may exclude or restrict the power.
-- src:7053 | (9) A company’s constitution may exclude or restrict the exercise of
-- src:7054 | a power conferred by this section.
@ref s 73(9) (src:7053-7054)
GIVEN `the constitution of the company excludes or restricts the exercise of a power conferred by section 73` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(9) the constitution may exclude or restrict the exercise of a power conferred by section 73` MEANS
    IF `the constitution of the company excludes or restricts the exercise of a power conferred by section 73`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company's constitution may exclude or restrict" -- a power the constitution has not used (grant ruling, limit 1)

-- (10) "redenomination".
-- src:7058 | (10) In this section and sections 73A and 73B, “redenomination”
-- src:7059 | means the conversion of share capital or any class of shares from one
-- src:7060 | currency to another.
@ref s 73(10) (src:7058-7060)
GIVEN `the conversion is of share capital or of any class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conversion is from one currency to another` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73(10) "redenomination" the conversion is a redenomination` MEANS
    IF `the conversion is of share capital or of any class of shares` AND `the conversion is from one currency to another`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): ""redenomination" means the conversion of share capital or any class of shares from one currency to another" (a "means" definition)

§ `Section 73A: effect of redenomination`

-- (1) what a redenomination does not affect.
-- src:7066 | 73A.—(1) A redenomination of shares does not affect —
-- src:7068 | (a) any rights or obligations of members under the company’s
-- src:7069 | constitution or any restrictions affecting members under
-- src:7070 | the company’s constitution; or
-- src:7072 | (b) any entitlement to dividends (including any entitlement to
-- src:7073 | dividends in a particular currency), voting rights and
-- src:7074 | liability in respect of amounts remaining unpaid on shares
-- src:7075 | (including liability in a particular currency).
@ref s 73A(1) (src:7066-7075)
DECLARE `s 73A(1) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 73A(1)(a) the rights or obligations of members under the company's constitution, or the restrictions affecting members under it`
    `s 73A(1)(b) the entitlement to dividends (including the entitlement to dividends in a particular currency)`
    `s 73A(1)(b) voting rights`
    `s 73A(1)(b) the liability in respect of amounts remaining unpaid on shares (including liability in a particular currency)`
    `s 73A(1) some other matter`

@ref s 73A(1) (src:7066-7075)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 73A(1) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A(1) the redenomination of shares affects the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 73A(1)(a) the rights or obligations of members under the company's constitution, or the restrictions affecting members under it` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A redenomination of shares does not affect -- (a) any rights or obligations of members under the company's constitution or any restrictions affecting members under the company's constitution"
    WHEN `s 73A(1)(b) the entitlement to dividends (including the entitlement to dividends in a particular currency)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A redenomination of shares does not affect ... (b) any entitlement to dividends (including any entitlement to dividends in a particular currency)"
    WHEN `s 73A(1)(b) voting rights` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A redenomination of shares does not affect ... (b) ... voting rights"
    WHEN `s 73A(1)(b) the liability in respect of amounts remaining unpaid on shares (including liability in a particular currency)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A redenomination of shares does not affect ... (b) ... liability in respect of amounts remaining unpaid on shares (including liability in a particular currency)"
    WHEN `s 73A(1) some other matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraphs name what a redenomination does not affect; any other matter is not covered

-- (2) the constitution for the purposes of (1) includes the terms of allotment or holding.
-- src:7082 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the reference to a company’s
-- src:7083 | constitution includes the terms on which any shares of the company
-- src:7084 | are allotted or held.
@ref s 73A(2) (src:7082-7084)
GIVEN `the thing is the constitution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is a term on which shares of the company are allotted or held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73A(2) the thing is within the company's constitution for the purposes of subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the thing is the constitution of the company` OR `the thing is a term on which shares of the company are allotted or held`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "includes the terms on which any shares of the company are allotted or held" -- "includes" lists without "only"

§ `Section 73B: notice of redenomination`

-- (1) the notice within 14 days after passing the resolution. Asked as "late": JUST TRUE where it was delivered after the 14th day, or is still not delivered after it.
-- src:7090 | 73B.—(1) Within 14 days after passing a resolution under
-- src:7091 | section 73, a company must deliver a notice in the specified form
-- src:7092 | to the Registrar for registration in relation to the redenomination.
@ref s 73B(1) (src:7090-7092)
GIVEN `the company has passed a resolution under section 73` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
      `a notice in the specified form has been delivered to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was delivered` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73B(1) the company is late in delivering the notice of redenomination to the Registrar` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company has passed a resolution under section 73`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 14 days after passing a resolution under section 73, a company must deliver a notice" -- a failed "after passing a resolution" (periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a)): the duty does not arise
    ELSE (IF `a notice in the specified form has been delivered to the Registrar`
          THEN (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the resolution was passed` `the day the notice was delivered` 14 Days
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 14 days after passing a resolution under section 73, a company must deliver a notice" -- delivered within the 14 days (a period the text fixes: periods ruling (a))
                ELSE JUST TRUE)
          ELSE (IF `the day on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the resolution was passed` 14 Days
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 14 days after passing a resolution" -- the 14 days have not yet run out (periods ruling (a))

DECLARE `s 73B act` IS ONE OF
    `s 73B(1) deliver to the Registrar a notice in the specified form of the redenomination`

@ref s 73B(1) (src:7090-7092)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 73B act`
`s 73B(1) a company must deliver the notice of redenomination to the Registrar within 14 days after passing the resolution` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 73B(1) deliver to the Registrar a notice in the specified form of the redenomination`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not deliver the notice of redenomination to the Registrar within 14 days after passing the resolution"

-- (2) what the notice must include.
-- src:7096 | (2) The notice must include the following information with respect
-- src:7097 | to the company’s share capital as redenominated by the resolution:
-- src:7099 | (a) the total number of issued shares in the company;
-- src:7101 | (b) the amount paid up or regarded as paid up and the amount
-- src:7102 | (if any) remaining unpaid on the total number of issued
-- src:7103 | shares in the company;
-- src:7105 | (c) the total amount of the company’s issued share capital; and
-- src:7107 | (d) for each class of shares —
-- src:7109 | (i) the particulars specified in subsection (3);
-- src:7111 | (ii) the total number of issued shares in the class;
-- src:7113 | (iii) the amount paid up or regarded as paid up and the
-- src:7114 | amount (if any) remaining unpaid on the total
-- src:7115 | number of issued shares in the class; and
-- src:7117 | (iv) the total amount of issued share capital of the class.
@ref s 73B(2) (src:7096-7117)
GIVEN `the notice states the total number of issued shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the amount paid up or regarded as paid up and the amount, if any, remaining unpaid on the total number of issued shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the total amount of the company's issued share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for each class of shares the notice states the particulars specified in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for each class of shares the notice states the total number of issued shares in the class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for each class of shares the notice states the amount paid up or regarded as paid up and the amount, if any, remaining unpaid on the total number of issued shares in the class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for each class of shares the notice states the total amount of issued share capital of the class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73B(2) the notice includes the information the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the notice states the total number of issued shares in the company`
      AND `the notice states the amount paid up or regarded as paid up and the amount, if any, remaining unpaid on the total number of issued shares in the company`
      AND `the notice states the total amount of the company's issued share capital`
      AND `for each class of shares the notice states the particulars specified in subsection (3)`
      AND `for each class of shares the notice states the total number of issued shares in the class`
      AND `for each class of shares the notice states the amount paid up or regarded as paid up and the amount, if any, remaining unpaid on the total number of issued shares in the class`
      AND `for each class of shares the notice states the total amount of issued share capital of the class`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must include the following information with respect to the company's share capital as redenominated by the resolution" (a duty not met, the subsection's own question)

-- (3) the particulars for each class.
-- src:7121 | (3) The particulars referred to in subsection (2)(d)(i) are —
-- src:7123 | (a) particulars of any voting rights attached to shares in the
-- src:7124 | class, including rights that arise only in certain
-- src:7125 | circumstances;
-- src:7127 | (b) particulars of any rights attached to shares in the class, as
-- src:7128 | respects dividends, to participate in a distribution;
-- src:7130 | (c) particulars of any rights attached to shares in the class, as
-- src:7131 | respects capital, to participate in a distribution (including
-- src:7132 | on a winding up of the company); and
-- src:7137 | (d) whether or not shares in the class are redeemable shares.
@ref s 73B(3) (src:7121-7137)
GIVEN `the notice states particulars of any voting rights attached to shares in the class, including rights that arise only in certain circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states particulars of any rights attached to shares in the class, as respects dividends, to participate in a distribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states particulars of any rights attached to shares in the class, as respects capital, to participate in a distribution (including on a winding up of the company)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states whether or not shares in the class are redeemable shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73B(3) the notice states the particulars the subsection specifies for the class` MEANS
    IF    `the notice states particulars of any voting rights attached to shares in the class, including rights that arise only in certain circumstances`
      AND `the notice states particulars of any rights attached to shares in the class, as respects dividends, to participate in a distribution`
      AND `the notice states particulars of any rights attached to shares in the class, as respects capital, to participate in a distribution (including on a winding up of the company)`
      AND `the notice states whether or not shares in the class are redeemable shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The particulars referred to in subsection (2)(d)(i) are -- (a) particulars of any voting rights ...; (b) ... dividends ...; (c) ... capital ...; and (d) whether or not shares in the class are redeemable shares" (the particulars the notice must give, the subsection's own question)

-- (4) the offence of default.
-- src:7141 | (4) If default is made in complying with this section, every officer
-- src:7142 | of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:7143 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $4,000 and to a
-- src:7144 | default penalty of $250.
@ref s 73B(4) (src:7141-7144)
DECLARE `s 73B(4) penalty` HAS
    `s 73B(4) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 73B(4) the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 73B(4) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 73B(4) a default penalty is also payable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 73B(4) the default penalty, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
@ref s 73B(4) (src:7141-7144)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 73B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 73B(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `default is made in complying with section 73B`
      AND `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "If default is made in complying with this section, every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts; it does not say the person is innocent of any other offence
@ref s 73B(4) (src:7141-7144)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 73B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 73B(4) penalty`
`s 73B(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 73B(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 73B` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 73B(4) penalty` OF 4000, 0, FALSE, TRUE, 250)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

